      {
        "alias": "P7",
        "source_id": "congressionalglo7395unit:741:par_000741_000006",
        "part_number": 5,
        "scan_leaf": 741,
        "role": "target",
        "raw": {
          "text": "He cannot give a license or indulgence to com- mit crime ; but after a crime is committed, all he has to do in his certificate is to specify par- ticularly the crime that has been committed and for which the pardon is granted. But it may well be denied that but for the act of Con- gress of July 17, 18G2, of which my friend from New Hampshire before me [Mr. Clark] was perhaps the chief draughtsman, the President would have any authority to grant a general pardon or amnestj\\ I must admit that that act is quite full. Let me refer to it. The thirteenth section is in these words :",
          "sha256": "f77d6de4e79ea615bc7c3a4823987f768a829a9c452386c87a3605007eb2b678"
        },
        "static": {
          "text": "He cannot give a license or indulgence to commit crime ; but after a crime is committed, all he has to do in his certificate is to specify particularly the crime that has been committed and for which the pardon is granted. But it may well be denied that but for the act of Congress of July 17, 18G2, of which my friend from New Hampshire before me [Mr. Clark] was perhaps the chief draughtsman, the President would have any authority to grant a general pardon or amnestj\\ I must admit that that act is quite full. Let me refer to it. The thirteenth section is in these words :",
          "sha256": "f8112d954cc61248d321cd82910e2c74919a47a48f867abcbeb4f393c470f1a4",
